<metadata>

  <!--
    TracingInterceptor.BaseBuilder<T : TracingInterceptor, R : BaseBuilder<T, R>> is an F-bounded
    generic, and its abstract build() returns T - erased to TracingInterceptor. DatadogInterceptor
    .Builder overrides it returning DatadogInterceptor. Java expresses that with a bridge method;
    C# has no covariant override, so the subclass fails to implement the abstract member (CS0534).

    Removing the abstract build() from the base is what keeps both builders useful: neither
    subclass is overriding anything any more, so each keeps its own precise return type and
    `new DatadogInterceptor.Builder(hosts).Build()` still hands back a DatadogInterceptor rather
    than something to downcast. The only thing lost is calling Build() through a BaseBuilder
    reference, which is not a shape anyone writes - BaseBuilder exists to share fluent setters.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.datadog.android.okhttp.trace']/class[@name='TracingInterceptor.BaseBuilder']/method[@name='build']" />


</metadata>
